        "detail": "Commit `88cfeb4` on `feature/sv-0317`.\n\n## Changes (4 files):\n\n1. **`app/hooks/useHelpShortcut.ts`** (new) — Custom hook with:\n   - `isHelpToggleKey()` pure predicate: returns true for `?` key when not in form controls (input/textarea/select/contentEditable)\n   - `isHelpCloseKey()` pure predicate: returns true for Escape\n   - `useHelpShortcut()` hook: manages boolean state, attaches document-level keydown listener on mount, cleans up on unmount. Returns `[isOpen, toggle]` tuple.\n\n2. **`app/hooks/useHelpShortcut.test.ts`** (new) — 9 unit tests covering:\n   - `?` key on generic element → true\n   - Non-`?` keys → false\n   - `?` on input/textarea/select/contentEditable → false\n   - Missing target edge case → true\n   - Escape → true / non-Escape → false\n\n3. **`app/hooks/index.ts`** — Added `useHelpShortcut` export to barrel\n\n4. **`app/routes/play.tsx`** — Wired hook into PlayLevel:\n   - Added `useHelpShortcut()` call\n   - Added inline help modal overlay (matching LevelComplete visual style: backdrop-blur, animate-fadeIn/scaleIn)\n   - Modal has role=dialog, aria-modal, aria-label for accessibility\n   - Backdrop click and close button both use toggle callback\n   - Updated import budget comment (hooks: 2 → 3)\n\n## Decisions:\n- Extracted pure predicates for testability without jsdom (project has no DOM test environment)\n- Used document-level listener (not element-level) since there are no inputs on the play screen currently, and the FORM_TAGS guard future-proofs it\n- Included inline placeholder modal content rather than waiting for the sibling HowToPlayModal task — the sibling task can replace the inline content with the full component\n\n## Validation: typecheck ✓, lint ✓ (pre-existing warning only), all 162 tests pass ✓"
